# Line endings are load-bearing, not cosmetic.
#
# `.thesis` world files and the lock manifest are content-addressed by SHA-256
# over their exact bytes. On a Windows checkout with the default
# core.autocrlf=true, git would rewrite every LF to CRLF, the strict canonical
# decoder would reject the file, and every world_hash in the committed
# regression corpus would break at once: surfacing in someone else's clone,
# long after the mistake.
#
# `text eol=lf` normalizes to LF on commit AND checks out as LF on every
# platform. Do NOT use `binary` here: it implies -diff, which would render
# every lock and regression-corpus change as "Binary files differ" and defeat
# the human review that anti-gaming rules 1 and 4 depend on.

*.thesis        text eol=lf
*.jsonl         text eol=lf
# Golden files are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE across a module boundary
# (internal/driver/testdata/golden_plan.json is the driver-plan wire format, and
# testdata/kvfixture carries the same bytes so both sides of the format are
# pinned). A CRLF rewrite on checkout would fail those tests on a fresh Windows
# clone and nowhere else. The fixture module already declares this rule; the
# root did not, which is the gap this line closes.
*.json          text eol=lf
# `**/` and not `.prothesis/lock`: a gitattributes pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to the directory holding the file, so the un-prefixed form matched the
# ROOT lock only and silently skipped testdata/kvfixture/.prothesis/lock, which
# is the one lock this repository actually commits. `git check-attr` reported no
# attributes at all for it, and it had been committed with CRLF. Found while
# regenerating that lock for D-060.
**/.prothesis/lock text eol=lf
# Observation bundles under docs/observations/ are byte-compared against the run
# directories they were copied from, and their records assert those hashes. The
# JSON and .thesis artifacts were already covered above; container logs (.log)
# and the provenance readbacks (.txt) were not, so on a fresh Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true they would check out as CRLF and stop matching. Found while
# committing OBS-LIVE-002, and it applies retroactively to OBS-LIVE-001.
*.log           text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.go            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
go.mod          text eol=lf
go.sum          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
LICENSE         text eol=lf
